  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1603.01 Maximum Sulfur Content of Liquid Fuels",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1603.01 Maximum Sulfur Content of Liquid Fuels.\n\n(a) JP-4 aviation fuel shall not exceed 0.40 percent sulfur by weight.\n\n(b) Aviation gasoline shall not exceed 0.05 percent sulfur by weight.\n\n(c) Kerosene-1 oil shall not exceed 0.04 percent sulfur by weight.\n\n(d) Kerosene-2 oil and Jet A, A-1, B, and JP-8 aviation fuels shall not exceed 0.30 percent sulfur by weight.\n\n(e) Used oil shall not exceed 2.00 percent sulfur by weight.\n\nSource. #6519-B, eff 5-29-97; ss by #8330, eff 4-23-05; ss by #10415, eff 9-24-13 (from Env-A 1604.01); ss by #12694, eff 12-22-18; ss by #13808, eff 11-18-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1600.html"
